As an aside ...

y'know what? Nethack is not fair AT ALL.  It gives wands of death to
the bad guys when it hasn't given you a single counter to you.  It
summons in mindflayers and master liches in traps that rip off your
armor and suck your brains dry in a round.  The damn wizard won't stay
dead, even if his body has been dumped in water, lava, fed to a vicious
dog.  Demogorgon pops in at the most inconvenient times.

There is never a moment in the game when the specter of unavoidable
death is not hanging over my character like the sword of Damocles.

Y'know what?  I like it that way. I PREFER it that way.  I have a
number of games that are "fair" that way, and they just don't hold my
interest as well. A lot of the fun of the game comes from the fact that
no matter how good you are, no matter how experienced you are, no
matter that you're a level-30 fighter with an AC of -75,  it is never
entirely risk-free.  That's why I'm still playing this stupid game
after fifteen years. 

